  "provenance": "Avila Labs OC-007 coupled cost search benchmark, frozen 2026-09-10 before any search ran. Pins OC-006's robinson-superpower-ap-v3-lowfield dataset (csv_sha256 043cbaab9a32da5de6394b136265835b9c5917e28861d0793544c5e3885f893b) with low_field_clamp_t 0.0501 and monotonicity_tolerance 0.002; evidence per the OC-006 audit: 3 of 3,010 pairs above 0.1% tolerance, worst +0.182% at 25 K, 0.05->0.07 T; a 0.2% tolerance covers that with headroom and stays far below any margin-relevant scale. Points with self_field_ratio > 1 are counted and reported; the OC-004 gate max_self_field_ratio 0.1 applies only to the limiting point of an otherwise-passing candidate. Costs (price_usd_per_m 30, scrap_fraction 0.1, assembly_cost_per_pancake_usd 500, joint_cost_usd 200 per pancake interface) are invented placeholders, not supplier data; the result is a modeled saving under a screening model, never a production claim. Pre-declared control expectation, checked against benchmarks/coupled/oc-007-control.json and reported either way: the two cases select the same optimum and give identical candidate statuses; only the basis counts of non-limiting low-field points differ. A disagreement is a finding, not something to reconcile by editing either case.",
